---
// AI referral source ledger — the mockup for key-features.md feature 1
// ("See which AI search tools and referrers drive leads and revenue").
//
// Replaces public/images/features/feature-1.png, which was the PowerAI TEMPLATE's stock
// "User Data Analytics" chart: a generic line-over-bars with years on the x-axis and "2.8M"
// on a tooltip. Nothing in it was this product, and none of it could be corrected by editing
// text, because it was pixels. Same reasoning as DashboardMockup.astro: built as markup so
// the labels stay greppable, it inherits real brand tokens instead of the template's violet,
// and it cannot silently drift out of date the way a screenshot does.
//
// ── WHY A LEDGER AND NOT ANOTHER BEFORE/AFTER ────────────────────────────────────────
// This section sits at homepage position 3, ABOVE both JourneyShowcase and
// DirectRescueShowcase. The hero's JourneyTrail already opens ChatGPT -> converted, and
// DirectRescueShowcase already runs the full "logged as Direct, it was actually ChatGPT"
// argument. A third before/after here would be the same story told three times in one
// scroll. So this panel shows the one thing neither of those shows: the RANKED source
// breakdown with a revenue column — which is bullet 2's claim ("stitches consideration
// phase AI chats to actual Stripe revenue") rather than bullet 1's detection claim.
//
// ── THE NUMBERS ARE ILLUSTRATIVE, AND THEY RECONCILE ─────────────────────────────────
// Sample data — a drawing of the product, never a claim about anyone's data (§6: never present
// sample figures as if they were real). Disclosed once per page in the footer ("Product visuals
// shown use illustrative data."), never as a per-card badge: design.md §29.8, the pattern #581
// shipped and key-features-mockups.test.js pins.
//
// They are also internally consistent, deliberately, so a reader who adds them up is not
// caught out:
//   • leads: 38 + 12 + 11 + 6 = 67, and 67 / 318 = 21.1% -> the footer's "21% of conversions".
//     318 is DashboardMockup.astro's Conversions KPI on this same page.
//   • ChatGPT's $3,840 is DashboardMockup's ChatGPT revenue row, unchanged, so the two
//     panels on one page agree rather than quietly contradicting.
// If you change a figure here, re-check both relationships. A mockup whose own arithmetic
// does not close is exactly the kind of detail this product cannot afford to get wrong.
//
// ── MARKS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Real brand logos, ported from dashboard/src/lib/brandLogos.jsx and committed locally at
// public/images/logos/. No favicon service is contacted at runtime — a privacy-first
// product must not make a third-party request per logo.
//
// OpenAI's is INLINE rather than an <img> for the same reason it is inline in
// DashboardMockup.astro and JourneyTrail.astro: openai.svg is monochrome and painted with
// fill="currentColor", which an <img> cannot inherit — loaded as an image it would resolve
// to black and vanish against this dark panel. The other three are multicolour and
// self-contained, so they load from their committed files.
const rows = [
  { source: "ChatGPT", mark: "openai", leads: "38", revenue: "$3,840" },
  { source: "Perplexity", mark: null, leads: "12", revenue: "$1,180" },
  { source: "Gemini", mark: "gemini", leads: "11", revenue: "$1,020" },
  { source: "Claude", mark: "anthropic", leads: "6", revenue: "$610" },
];

// ── WHAT THE MOTION MAY AND MAY NOT DEPICT ───────────────────────────────────────────
// The rows above are the settled, ranked reading order, and the count-up targets below are
// PARSED from those exact strings rather than restated as numbers. Two reasons, and the second
// is the load-bearing one:
//
//   1. key-features-mockups.test.js reads this file as TEXT, matching the quoted lead and
//      revenue fields above to reconcile 38+12+11+6=67 against DashboardMockup's 318
//      conversions and the footer's 21%. Restating them as numbers would break that pinning
//      while changing nothing a visitor sees.
//
//      That regex counts every match in the file, not just the array — so do not spell either
//      field name followed by a quoted figure anywhere in this comment block. Writing one out
//      as an example here made the file parse as five rows and reddened the test; the shape is
//      described in prose for that reason, not for style.
//
//   2. The reveal staggers DOWN the existing order and the figures count up to their own
//      values. It deliberately does NOT animate rows sorting themselves into rank — nothing
//      here computes a ranking, so a sort animation would have to start from a scrambled order
//      that exists nowhere in the data, and design.md §37.1's product-mechanic row bars motion
//      that dramatises a mechanic the component does not perform. Stagger depicts ranked
//      reading order, which is true; re-sorting would depict a computation, which is not.
//
// Making the ranking genuinely computed (numbers, a sort, a derived 21%) is a real improvement
// and is logged as separate future work — it is a data change, not a motion change, and belongs
// in a PR that updates the pinning tests alongside it.
const counts = rows.map((r) => ({
  leads: Number(r.leads.replace(/,/g, "")),
  revenue: Number(r.revenue.replace(/[$,]/g, "")),
}));
---

<div class="relative z-1 overflow-hidden rounded-[20px] border border-[#3D3830] bg-[#1F2323]">
  <!-- Header -->
  <div
    class="flex h-[44px] items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b border-white/10 bg-[#1B1F1F] px-4"
  >
    <span class="truncate text-xs font-bold text-[#F2F4F3]">AI referral sources</span>
  </div>

  <!-- Ledger -->
  <div class="p-4">
    <div
      class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto_auto] items-center gap-x-4 pb-2 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-[#7C7568]"
    >
      <span>Source</span>
      <span class="text-right">Leads</span>
      <span class="text-right">Revenue</span>
    </div>

    {
      rows.map((r, i) => (
        <div
          data-ledger-row
          class:list={[
            "grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto_auto] items-center gap-x-4 border-t border-[#3D3830] py-2.5 text-xs font-bold transition-colors",
            i === 0 ? "rounded-xl border-primary/30 bg-primary/8 px-2" : "",
          ]}
        >
          <span class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2 text-[#F2F4F3]">
            {r.mark ? (
              <span
                class="flex h-6 w-6 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-white/10 bg-[#282C2C]"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                {r.mark === "openai" ? (
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="h-3.5 w-3.5">
                    <path d="M22.28 9.82a5.97 5.97 0 0 0-.51-4.91 6.04 6.04 0 0 0-6.5-2.9A6.07 6.07 0 0 0 4.98 4.18a5.97 5.97 0 0 0-3.98 2.9 6.05 6.05 0 0 0 .74 7.1 5.97 5.97 0 0 0 .51 4.91 6.04 6.04 0 0 0 6.5 2.9 5.97 5.97 0 0 0 4.5 2.01 6.04 6.04 0 0 0 5.79-4.23 5.97 5.97 0 0 0 3.98-2.9 6.04 6.04 0 0 0-.74-7.05zm-9.06 12.66a4.48 4.48 0 0 1-2.87-1.04l.14-.08 4.78-2.76a.78.78 0 0 0 .39-.68v-6.74l2.02 1.17a.07.07 0 0 1 .04.05v5.58a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-4.5 4.5zM3.56 18.16a4.47 4.47 0 0 1-.54-3.02l.14.08 4.78 2.76a.77.77 0 0 0 .78 0l5.84-3.37v2.33a.07.07 0 0 1-.03.06l-4.83 2.79a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-6.14-1.63zM2.3 7.7a4.47 4.47 0 0 1 2.36-1.97V11.39a.77.77 0 0 0 .39.68l5.81 3.36-2.02 1.16a.07.07 0 0 1-.07 0l-4.83-2.8a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-1.64-6.14zm16.6 3.86l-5.84-3.39 2.02-1.16a.07.07 0 0 1 .07 0l4.83 2.79a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-.68 8.12v-5.69a.77.77 0 0 0-.4-.67zm2-3.02l-.14-.08-4.77-2.78a.78.78 0 0 0-.78 0L9.36 9.05V6.72a.07.07 0 0 1 .03-.06l4.83-2.79a4.5 4.5 0 0 1 6.68 4.66zM8.26 12.65l-2.02-1.17a.07.07 0 0 1-.04-.06V5.85a4.5 4.5 0 0 1 7.38-3.46l-.14.08-4.78 2.76a.78.78 0 0 0-.39.68zm1.1-2.37l2.6-1.5 2.6 1.5v3l-2.6 1.5-2.6-1.5z" fill="#F2F4F3" />
                  </svg>
                ) : (
                  <img
                    src={`/images/logos/${r.mark}.svg`}
                    alt=""
                    width="14"
                    height="14"
                    class="h-3.5 w-3.5"
                    loading="lazy"
                    decoding="async"
                  />
                )}
              </span>
            ) : (
              <span class="h-6 w-6 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
            )}
            <span class="truncate">{r.source}</span>
          </span>
          <span
            class="text-right tabular-nums text-[#D5D0C3]"
            data-ledger-count
            data-count-final={r.leads}
            data-count-to={counts[i].leads}
            data-count-delay={i * 80}>{r.leads}</span>
          <span
            class="text-right tabular-nums text-primary"
            data-ledger-count
            data-count-final={r.revenue}
            data-count-to={counts[i].revenue}
            data-count-prefix="$"
            data-count-delay={i * 80}>{r.revenue}</span>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <!-- Footer callout -->
  <div class="mx-4 mb-4 rounded-2xl border border-[#3D3830] bg-[#282C2C] p-3.5">
    <div class="mb-1 text-[10px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#A8AFAF]">
      AI attribution
    </div>
    <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold leading-normal text-[#DDE4E4]">
      AI referrals drove <span class="font-black text-primary">21%</span> of conversions this
      period. Most analytics label these as direct traffic.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  import { countUp } from "@/lib/countUp";
  import { revealOnScroll } from "@/lib/revealOnScroll";

  // Both helpers query ALL matches, per #582 — this panel renders once on the homepage today,
  // but KeyFeatures.astro also imports it, so reviving that partial would put two on the page
  // and a first-match-only binding would leave the second one dead.
  //
  // revealOnScroll owns the row hide at runtime rather than baking opacity:0 into the markup
  // (#530), and carries the viewport-checked sweep that recovers a row a dead observer would
  // otherwise strand invisible. The figures use countUp instead, whose failure mode is the
  // opposite and benign: the true number is already in the DOM, so nothing firing means no
  // animation rather than no data.
  function initLedgerMotion() {
    const ease = [0.22, 0.72, 0.28, 1] as const; // design.md §37.1 standard easing
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-ledger-row]").forEach((row, i) => {
      revealOnScroll(
        row,
        { opacity: [0, 1], transform: ["translateY(8px)", "translateY(0)"] },
        { duration: 0.4, ease, delay: i * 0.08 },
      );
    });
    countUp("[data-ledger-count]");
  }

  if (document.readyState === "loading") {
    document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", initLedgerMotion);
  } else {
    initLedgerMotion();
  }
  document.addEventListener("astro:after-swap", initLedgerMotion);
</script>
